-R . Lib
-R ../../update-core/proofs-coq Lib

# umbra-chain-core — the blob-body half of the verifiable secure enclave update
# (issue #58). `Primitives.v` and `AeneasLoopShim.v` are NOT duplicated here:
# they are loaded out of update-core/proofs-coq (second -R above), because
# Chain_Compose.v Requires update-core's `Update_Crypto` and two files of the
# same logical name in one load path would clash. Build update-core FIRST.
#
# Regenerate the extracted files with ../extract.sh (re-applies the manual
# patches: loop-shim import + Coq-8.18 binder rewrite + opaque u32 codecs +
# the total mk_array4 replacing the backend's inconsistent mk_array axiom).

Chain_Types.v
Chain_FunsExternal.v
Chain_Funs.v
# Value layer over the EXTRACTED body: what `block_preimage` puts where (the
# per-byte window laws), when `ct_eq32_at` returning true forces byte equality,
# and the congruence of `blob_block_count` in the header bytes it reads.
Chain_Value.v
# The fold as an inductive trace, the refinement of the extracted loop into one,
# and the collision-extraction lemma (no injectivity assumption anywhere).
Chain_Trace.v
# THE TARGET THEOREM: two blobs accepted by the same chain gate against the same
# authenticated header.hmac either agree byte-for-byte on the whole folded region
# or exhibit an explicit HMAC collision.
Chain_Body.v
# Composition with umbra-update-core's P2: acceptance of two packages under one
# armed nonce pins the header.hmac window, which is exactly the chain gate's
# reference value.
Chain_Compose.v
# The honest negative: exactly which blob bytes the gate cannot see.
Chain_Residual.v
# Non-vacuity: the gate's `true` branch is not dead code — a matching
# measurement IS accepted, so the target theorem's hypothesis is met by every
# honestly-signed blob.
Chain_Reachable.v
